A||||13||batboy||Grand Prix GT Shopping (final chapter?)||||12||
Z||000000||batboy||10-14-2000||10:10 PM||||I've been searching for just the "right" Pontiac Grand Prix for nearly two months now. I needed a cool, sporty, late model, low mileage, low maintenance, daily driver, so I could retire my Fieros to weekend cruises so I would quit racking so much miles on them. Things were breaking down faster than I could repair them on my two primary Fieros and my Suburban was killing me on gas bills.<P>Well today, after two months of looking, I found my car (subject to credit union approval of course). The pic was taken about two minutes after it started raining. Of course I didn't think to get the camera out when the sun was still out. This car drives and handles like a wet dream.<P>It's a 1998 Pontiac Grand Prix GT coupe (2 door), dark metallic forest green, less than 23,000 miles, one owner, pampered, garage kept, mint condition, it looks and drives like brand new, plus it still has some of the remaining factory warranty left.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GP-98-GT-mint.jpg">  <P>Here is a list of the options...it's "loaded" as they say in the car biz. I've never had a fancy car like this before. It's like a cross between a Fiero and a Cadillac.<P>3800 series II V6 Engine, Auto 4-Speed Transmission, Air Conditioning, 16 inch Alloy Wheels, Rear Spoiler, Anti-Lock Brakes, Center Console, Cruise Control, Dual Air Bags, Fog Lights, Intermittent Wipers, Power Brakes, Power Door Locks, Power Mirrors, Power Steering, Power Windows, Six-way Power Seat, CD Player (with built-in equalizer), Premium 8 Speaker Sound System with amp, Steering Wheel Mounted Stereo Controls, Rear Window Defroster, Remote Trunk Release, Tachometer, Tilt Steering Wheel, Traction Control System, Leather Seats, Heads Up Display, Keyless Entry, Alarm System, Power Moonroof (with sun shade), and Premium Lighting Package (includes auto dimming rear-view mirror).<P>Wow! Sorry, but I just HAD to brag a little before the realization of how far in debt I'm getting sinks completely in (even if it is way below book value, it's still a hunk of change).<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-14-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000001||Cheever2||10-14-2000||10:58 PM||||Looks just like the one Nolan Ryan drives.  He passed me last year, that's how I know. <P>Why not?  It's a Pontiac.  Besides, save the Fieros for the good stuff.  I think you're gonna like it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-15-2000||12:28 AM||||Nice looking Grand Prix!! I started using my Fiero as a weekend cruiser 2 years ago. Yes less things break and It stays cleaner longer.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Ozzy||10-15-2000||12:39 AM||||That's a nice ride BB!<P>Don't tell my wife; She likes the Fiero and all but has been bugging me for a long time for a nice Grand Prix. Once I get the payments down on our truck I'm gonna buy her one similar to that. Everything except the Auto tranny; She luvs stick shift.<P>Congrats!<P>Ozzy||||reg||10
Z||000004||batboy||10-15-2000||01:34 AM||||Thanks all. Hey Ozzy, sorry to disappoint you and your wife, but the Grand Prix only comes in an automatic. You can get a 5 speed in the Grand Am GT mated with the 3400 engine (1999 and newer). I thought about it, but decided I had to have the GP GT with the 3800 motor.<P>Obviously, I decided not to buy that 2000 GP Daytona 500 pace car I was looking at. This car I'm interested in now is over $10,000 cheaper. I had a major reality check on what I could truly afford right now!<P>Dark green seems to be "in" right now. I ended up looking at five in that color. It's pretty nice, but I like the metallic bronzemist the best. There is a dark red (almost maroon) that is nice too. However, bright red, white, and black Grand Prixes are common place and boring. When I'm looking at used cars, color is not a big issue, although I was sort of avoiding black.<P>I think those 225-60-16 tires need upgraded to a set of fatter, lower profile, white lettered, BFG Comp T/A rubber. Any other suggestions for mods? No supercharger or performance mods, gotta let the Batmobile be top driveway dog in that respect.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Coconut||10-15-2000||01:56 AM||||Hey, Nice score Batboy!<P>Enjoy the new ride, she looks like a beauty! You know, when we went looking through the Grand Ams at our local Pontiac dealer, GtGirl & I were mildly shocked to find out that you can't get a stick with  the V6 Grand Ams or the Grand Prixs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">.<BR>What the heck is Pontiac thinking? I'm sure there are still plenty of prospective customers who would PREFER to mix their own gears. Other than that, the car is a dream for GTGirl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> she just loves it! I'm sure that you'll get the same satisfaction that we are. ENJOY!!<P>Cruisin' On,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||batboy||10-15-2000||08:47 AM||||Ok, dang it, I've been proven wrong again. Coconut it right about the 5 speed tranny being unavailable with the V6 even in the Grand Am. The 5 speed is only available with the standard 4 cylinder in the Grand Am and not offered in the Grand Prix models at all.<P>First thing I need to do is to after I officially own this GT is to get some buxom supermodel on a sunny day to pose next to it for a much better pic.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||10-15-2000||10:26 AM||||Keep in mind my Grand Prix is going to be a daily driver, so I don't want to get too carried away. But, here are a couple mods I am already planning, other than eventually getting better, maybe bigger tires.<P>Move coolant bottle, etc. under the hood like Pontiac began doing in 1999 for better air flow and add a cold air induction box with K & N filter, plus maybe a 180 degree Hypertech thermostat. There are claims that these mod often adds over 10 HP, but since the 1999 and newer 3800 normally aspirated engines are rated 200 HP (5 more HP than before), I'd be pleased to just break the 200 pony mark and call it good enough.<P>Not much to improve on with the exterior, except to find a place to slip in a pair of those cool, high tech, little round projector beam Blazertech driving lights and maybe add a pair of smoke tinted headlight covers (see pic). They quickly remove for night driving.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.grandprixstore.com/Merchant2/graphics/00000001/hdltcvrsl.jpg"> <P>Inside, the carpet might need a little spot cleaning. Nothing wrong with the leather though. I think a real wood dash trim kit would look great and add an exotic look.<P>Last but not least, a couple small improvements to the sound system (it already has a kick butt CD stereo with 8 speakers). There, now I have...a total babe magnet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||10-15-2000||12:51 PM||||I admit, the headlight blackout kits do look cool on some cars..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I didn't know they were easily removable for night driving, as most of the cars I've seen them on, kept them on all the time. which is nice when they're driving at you on the highway at night... their lights aren't as bright as the others.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000009||Monkeyman||10-15-2000||03:41 PM||||Two thoughts...<P>First, I think you should lower it just a little.<P>Second, now you can reliably drive to Canada.  You should actually meet the giggle girl.<P>Fourth, if you ever total the car (God forbid) you can put most of those parts into one of your Fieros.  3800, 4spd auto, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DJRice||10-16-2000||09:50 PM||||Hmm...Ill take the heads up display and the leather shifter handle.  <P>What?<P>Your not parting it out?<P>You mean I'm not in "The Mall"?<P>I hate it when that happens....<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula||10-16-2000||10:51 PM||||as a former rice burner owner, I must say that headlight covers + night = BAD visibility.  and they become a pain really quick to keep taking off||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||10-16-2000||11:35 PM||||A couple steps closer to Grand Prix excitement. The credit union says no problem with the loan. I'm giving the owner a down payment tomorrow after work. The owner has began the process of getting the lien released on the title from his credit union and transfered to mine. We made an appointment to close the deal on Friday afternoon. I'll be kruising Kansas all weekend in my new (to me) Pontiac GT. Yippee!<P>Formula, yeah you're probably right about the headlight covers. Maybe I'll wait until next summer when the days are long and I don't do much night driving.||||reg||6
Z||000013||Raydar||10-17-2000||10:23 AM||||Batboy, Nice score!<BR>I've lusted after a GP on and off for a year or two. Looks like you're getting a good one.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||14
